PROJECT NAME: PixGallery

TAGLINE: Discover. Explore. Enjoy.

Act as a senior full-stack developer, UI/UX designer, database architect, and web security expert. Build a complete, professional, mobile-first photo gallery website named PixGallery with a beautiful, colorful, modern design.

The website must be fully functional, responsive, secure, and production-ready. Do not create just a static design or a visual prototype. All buttons, forms, uploads, admin functions, database operations, and photo interactions must work correctly.

1. WEBSITE DESIGN AND BRAND IDENTITY

Website Name: PixGallery

Tagline: Discover. Explore. Enjoy.

Language: English only.

Design Style: Premium, modern, colorful, elegant, and professional.

Color Theme:

- Pink
- Blue
- Purple
- Red
- Cyan
- Gradient combinations of multiple colors
- Dark backgrounds with colorful accents
- White text and clean typography where appropriate

Use a beautiful combination of pink, blue, purple, and multicolor gradients. Avoid excessive visual clutter.

Use modern typography, smooth transitions, rounded cards, subtle shadows, attractive buttons, and professional spacing.

The website must look excellent on Android phones, iPhones, tablets, laptops, and desktop computers.

2. PHOTO GALLERY LAYOUT

Create a visually attractive photo gallery with a vertical 9:16 aspect ratio for photo cards.

Requirements:

- Display photos in a modern, responsive gallery grid.
- Every gallery card should use a 9:16 portrait layout.
- Use object-fit: cover for visually attractive image previews.
- Display a white play-style icon overlay on each photo card.
- Use a clean white circular icon with a subtle shadow.
- Add a smooth hover effect on desktop and touch-friendly interactions on mobile.
- Display the photo title beneath or over the image using an attractive layout.
- Allow users to open any photo in a dedicated photo-viewing page or modal.
- Show the full photo title and description when a photo is opened.
- Display the photo publication date.
- Include a related photos section.
- Add pagination or a Load More button.
- Avoid loading every image at once.
- Use lazy loading and optimized image sizes for faster performance.
- Do not display fake demo photos or placeholder posts in production.
- Display only photos published by the administrator.

The white play-style icon is a visual design element for opening the photo. It does not mean every photo must contain a video.

3. WEBSITE NAVIGATION

Create a professional navigation system containing:

- Home
- Latest Photos
- Popular
- Categories
- Search
- About Us
- Contact Us

Include a beautiful PixGallery logo and a responsive mobile navigation menu.

The homepage should display:

